  "step_3": "The decision reason requires comparing variances and preferring the lottery with the larger variance. In this case, Lottery A has a higher variance than Lottery B, so the reason would prefer A. However, the individual chose B and justified the choice by saying it had 'less risk.' This justification does not refer to variance or any measure of dispersion. Instead, it reflects a different concept of risk — possibly a subjective or intuitive sense of risk, which may not align with variance-based reasoning. There is no mention of variance, calculations, or comparison of dispersion. Therefore, the individual did not use the variance-based decision reason. The justification is inconsistent with the rule of the decision reason. The individual’s reasoning is based on a different principle (perceived risk), not on variance. Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
